Jonadab the Unsightly One <jonadab.theunsightlyone@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> One bones change I'd like to see is the ability for the game to save
> more than one set of bones for the same level -- on loading, then, it
> would select one of them at random. This would result in a small
> increase in the number of bones levels you'd encounter (because, if
> somebody dies on a level for which there are bones already, and they
> leave bones, the number of bones files available in total would increase
> by one; somebody could still get the ones that, with the way things are
> done now, get overwritten),

In UnNetHack I didn't do it this way as this would have meant to add
lots of code for reading/writing/existence-checking files, as there
is no help in the NetHack code itself for dealing with files and the
low level C stuff is just so error prone.

It was much easier just to fiddle with the bones name. Adding a simple
number computed from the starting time of the current game. But this
also means that you don't increase the numbers of the existing bones
files.

> but more interestingly it would mean that the bones you would get
> might not be from the most recent time somebody died there. The
> bones levels could be loaded out of order.

This is the feature that I wanted to have.

This also means that when you die and immediately play again and get
to the same depth where you died, it is much less likely that you hit
your own bones.

> That, and wizard bones should only be loaded in wizard mode, and explore
> mode bones should only be loaded in explore mode. (Wizard mode bones are
> irrelevant on a public server, of course.)

NAO doesn't allow explore mode IIRC.

> Oh, and when somebody on a public server encounters bones from one of my
> games, it would be cool if I could get notified by email after the fact,
> [...]

The bot in #unnethack announces the *kill* of a bones ghost.

